    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and wrote a 37-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with all 37 tests green. Each client keeps a time-ordered list of `(time, cost)` records, and entries older than `window_seconds` are dropped when a method reads them. `allow` rejects without recording anything when the cost would exceed the limit. `remaining` returns `limit` minus the units still in use. `retry_after` walks the live records oldest-first and returns the time until the first expiry that makes the cost fit. Argument validation follows the spec, including rejecting `bool` for `limit` and `cost`. The backwards-time check tracks the largest `now` any method has accepted, across all clients. I also reject a `now` that is not a number only implicitly, through the comparisons, and I did not add any extra validation for it. I did not create any other files or install anything.",
